# Competency question: "What are the lawful sidedness values a p-value may declare?"
# Exercises the enumerated math:Sidedness code list: the tail/side of a p-value is fixed by
# one of a closed set of individuals (never a free literal), each asserted a math:Sidedness in
# module.ttl. The reasoning-free query enumerates the members of the code list and binds the
# code-list class itself as a constant, so the answer names every lawful value AND the
# math:Sidedness type that closes them. Over the merged ontology the answer is exactly the six
# individuals {math:oneSidedAlternative, math:twoSidedAlternative, math:greaterAlternative,
# math:lessAlternative, math:exactTail, math:midPTail}, each of kind math:Sidedness.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?sidedness ?class WHERE {
    ?sidedness a math:Sidedness .
    BIND(math:Sidedness AS ?class)
}
ORDER BY ?sidedness
